`generate` writes a block once when the same module, scope, binding and
content reach it twice, for example from a native and a Melange copy of one
module. Blocks with the same content in two different modules are different
blocks: the module name is part of the class, so both are kept.

  $ refmt --parse re --print ml input_a.re > output_a.ml
  $ ../../standalone.exe --impl output_a.ml -o output_a.ml
  $ refmt --parse re --print ml input_b.re > output_b.ml
  $ ../../standalone.exe --impl output_b.ml -o output_b.ml
  $ styled-ppx.generate output_a.ml output_b.ml > styles.css
  $ cat styles.css
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  .css-4vffj8{display:flex;}
  .css-15g1gu9{color:blue;}
  .css-hv04e2{margin:10px;}
  .css-f8qyjw{display:flex;}
  .css-1kfgxy4{color:blue;}
  .css-gc88kl{padding:20px;}

The same module compiled twice (here, copied to a second folder) is written
once.

  $ mkdir copy && cp output_a.ml copy/output_a.ml
  $ styled-ppx.generate output_a.ml copy/output_a.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  .css-4vffj8{display:flex;}
  .css-15g1gu9{color:blue;}
  .css-hv04e2{margin:10px;}
